6,Mvanip,https://docs.verbix.com/EndangeredLanguages/Mvanip,"Language family: Niger-Congo, Atlantic-Congo, Volta-Congo, Benue-Congo, Bantoid, Northern, Mambiloid, Mambila-Konja, Magu-Kamkam-Kila (SIL classification). Number of speakers: 100. Vulnerability: Threatened. Script: More information: Mvanip is spoken in Nigeria, Africa.",Mvanip,Niger-Congo
7,"Full text of ""enwiki-Mvanip_language-20200726.pdf""",https://archive.org/stream/enwiki-Mvanip_language-20200726.pdf/enwiki-Mvanip_language-20200726_djvu.txt,"Mvanip (Mvano), or Magu, is a minor Mambiloid language of Nigeria. Despite the small number of speakers, language use is vigorous. Ethnologue classifies Mvanip as threatened.",Mvanip,Niger-Congo
